GraphQL is a query language and server side runtime execution system for fulfilling queries on existing data
GraphQL provides schema to get the data
GraphQL is very fast and flexible
GraphQL provides schema to get the data from different tables/databases/apis
From application UI single calls is made to graphql and graphql talks to different apis to get only the data required in UI
Data is not stored in graphql
it understands the defined syntax query

Advantages:
Performance
Over fetching the data avoided

GraphQL type has data type - similar to java classes
example For author type you can ask details like id, author name, author age, author address, author posts

Once the developer develops graphql in backend, immediately frontend url will be exposed and available

Graphql can retrieve the data and also create the data in backend

syntax:
query{
//character(characterid: int!) ! is mandatory field
character(characterid: 8){ //for character with id 8 get the details like name
	name
}
location(locationid: 8){ 
	country
}

characters(filter: {name="Rahul"}){
info { //not scalar, info is type and from info type give the values required
    count
}
}
}

In graphql response fields can be dynamic along with value i.e request only required response fields
in rest api, response values only can be dynamic
query variables

{
"characterid": 8
locationid: 8
}
query($characterid: Int!){
character($characterid){ //for character with id 8 get the details like name
	name
}

}

GraphQL Mutations - Used to Create data

mutation{

createlocation(location: {name: "Aus", })
{
id //to get id for above
}

}

mutation is hybrid - creates and gets the data
